Package: kpe
Title: Estimating the Value of Personalized Treatment Assignment
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Emma", "Brunskill", email = "ebrun@cs.stanford.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2200-0019")),
    person("Zhaoqi", "Li", email = "zli9@stanford.edu", role = "aut"))
Description: Point estimate, confidence interval, and one-sided p-value for
    the personalization effect -- the expected outcome difference between
    the best personalized policy and the best single treatment applied to
    everyone. Implements the K-Fold Personalization Estimator of
    Li and Brunskill (2026). Supports binary and multi-arm discrete
    treatments, pluggable reward, contextual-policy, and best-arm
    learners, and is robust to mild misspecification of the plug-in
    models.
